# Codexeron API

Welcome to the official Codexeron API documentation.

The Codexeron API powers the internal services of the Codexeron platform. It is designed to provide secure communication between Codexeron applications, services, and future official integrations.

> **Notice**
>
> The Codexeron API is **not publicly available** in the current release. Public API access is not part of the current roadmap and may only be introduced for selected enterprise partners or official integrations in future versions.

---

# Overview

The Codexeron API is an internal service layer used by the Codexeron ecosystem.

Its primary purpose is to provide secure, reliable, and scalable communication between official Codexeron services.

---

# Current Usage

The API is currently intended for internal platform components such as:

- Codexeron Marketplace
- Administration Panel
- License Management
- Payment Services
- Notification Services
- Future Mobile Applications
- Future Desktop Applications

Third-party access is currently unavailable.

---

# API Design Principles

The Codexeron API is designed with the following principles:

- Security First
- Performance
- Reliability
- Scalability
- Maintainability
- Consistency

---

# Security

Security is a core requirement of every API component.

The platform follows these principles:

- HTTPS-only communication
- Secure authentication
- Request validation
- Access control
- Audit logging
- Rate limiting where required

Internal services follow the same security standards used throughout the Codexeron platform.

---

# Versioning

Internal API services follow Semantic Versioning.

Example:

```
v1
v2
v3
```

Breaking changes are introduced only in major versions.

---

# Future Availability

While the API is currently reserved for internal platform services, future versions of Codexeron may introduce limited API access for:

- Enterprise customers
- Official partners
- Official SDKs
- Mobile applications
- Desktop applications

No public API release is currently planned.

---

# Documentation Scope

This section documents the architecture and security principles of the Codexeron API.

Additional documentation will be published only if external API access becomes available in future releases.

